#
# Sensor  drivers configuration
#
menuconfig SENSORS_FINGERPRINT
	bool "Finger Print Sensor devices"
	help
	  Say Y here, and a list of sensors drivers will be displayed.
	  Everything that didn't fit into the other categories is here. This option
	  doesn't affect the kernel.
	  If unsure, say Y.

config SENSORS_FPRINT_SECURE
	tristate "fingerprint sensor support"
	default n
	help
	  If you say yes here you get support for Trustzone.
	  In case of user binary, fingerprint sensor operates within trustzone.
	  If this feature enabled, spi communication is controlled by Trusted Application.
	  Then it should be enabled in the user binary.

config SENSORS_FINGERPRINT_32BITS_PLATFORM_ONLY
	tristate "Fingerprint sensor supports only 32bits platform"
	default n
	help
	  If you say yes here the non TZ device driver will only supports
	  32bits platform.
	  In case of Exynos7580, this feature should be enabled.
	  And you should be use the compat_ioctl not the unlocked_ioctl.

config SENSORS_VFS7XXX
	tristate "VFS7XXX fingerprint sensor support"
	default n
	help
	  Fingerprint sensor driver.
	  If you say yes here you get support for viper2 sensor.
	  Viper2 is the touch type fingerprint sensor.
	  Viper2 82E5 module can support WOG mode.

config SENSORS_VFS8XXX
	tristate "VFS8XXX fingerprint sensor support"
	default n
	help
	  Fingerprint sensor driver.
	  If you say yes here you get support for Namsan sensor.
	  Namsan is the touch type fingerprint sensor.
	  Namsan module can support WOF mode.

config SENSORS_ET5XX
	tristate "ET5XX fingerprint sensor supprot"
	default n
	help
	  Fingerprint sensor driver.
	  If you say yes here you get support for ET5XX sensor.
	  ET5XX is the touch type fingerprint sensor.
	  ET5XX module can support WOF mode.

config SENSORS_ET7XX
	stristate "ET7XX fingerprint sensor support"
	default n
	help
	  If you say yes here you get support for Egistec's
	  fingerprint sensor ET7XX.  This is the symbol name the stock
	  exynos7885 A30s kernel config uses, so it must stay spelled
	  exactly this way or the stock config stops resolving.
	
	  ET7XX is Egistec's optical under-display sensor family
	  (ET711A / ET713A / ET715).  The driver binds to the DT
	  compatible string "etspi,et7xx" and probes as an SPI device.
	  The A30s carries an ET715.
	
	  This symbol is MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE with SENSORS_ET5XX above.
	  Both build objects that export the SAME global symbols --
	  etspi_Interrupt_Init, etspi_Interrupt_Free, etspi_Interrupt_Abort,
	  etspi_fps_interrupt_poll, etspi_platformInit, etspi_platformUninit
	  and fpsensor_goto_suspend -- and both link built-in into vmlinux,
	  so enabling the two together is a duplicate-definition link
	  failure, not a runtime conflict.  There is deliberately no
	  depends on / select between them: kconfig would then silently drop
	  one of the two symbols, which is the failure mode that hides
	  itself.  Keep the pairing explicit in the defconfig instead.  The
	  correct pairing for this board, and the one the stock config uses,
	  is SENSORS_ET7XX=y with SENSORS_ET5XX unset.
	
	  Coexists freely with SENSORS_VFS7XXX and SENSORS_VFS8XXX: those
	  use a vfsspi_ symbol prefix and claim no overlapping global.
	  VFS7XXX has no object at all in this tree, and VFS8XXX is the
	  9810-era Namsan part, which is not what this die carries.
